<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Dona Paula View Point Guide" description="Privacy policy for the independent Dona Paula View Point Guide." path="/privacy/"><section class="section"><div class="wrap prose max-w-4xl"><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1 class="serif text-5xl font-bold text-[#072e33]">Privacy Policy</h1><p><b>Last updated: August 2026</b></p><h2>Information we collect</h2><p>We collect only the minimum data reasonably necessary to operate and improve this information website. This may include browser and server-log data such as IP address, browser type, device information and pages visited; cookie or similar preference data; and information you voluntarily provide if you contact the project by email or another clearly identified contact channel.</p><h2>How we use information</h2><ul><li>To improve site content, accessibility and visitor experience.</li><li>To understand aggregate traffic and usage patterns.</li><li>To respond to requests or correspondence.</li><li>To protect the service and comply with applicable legal obligations.</li></ul><h2>Google Analytics</h2><p>Google Analytics 4 is configured only after you opt in to analytics cookies. We use the measurement ID supplied for this project and request IP anonymisation where supported. You can withdraw analytics consent at any time on the <a class="link" href="/cookies/">Cookie Settings</a> page.</p><h2>Google Maps and external resources</h2><p>The site embeds Google Maps for location context. Loading an embedded map can cause Google to receive technical data according to Google’s own policies. Some photographs may be loaded from licensed third-party image hosts; those hosts may receive standard web-request information.</p><h2>Your rights</h2><p>Depending on the law that applies to you, including GDPR-style rights where relevant, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict processing of personal data, object to certain processing, withdraw consent, and complain to a competent supervisory authority.</p><h2>Data retention</h2><p>We retain operational data only for as long as reasonably needed for the purposes described above or to meet legal and security obligations. Browser-side cookie preferences remain on your device until you clear them or change your settings.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>This site is a general visitor-information resource and is not designed to knowingly collect personal data from children.</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy when the website, applicable law or third-party services change. The month shown at the top identifies the current published version.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
